**Claudally {{VERSION}}** — Tally Prime ERP for Claude, and any MCP client.

### Install

Download `{{FILE}}` and run it. The wizard takes a Windows box from nothing installed to a running service; most values auto-detect. Node.js is bundled.

Requires Tally Prime (Silver or Gold) with the XML server enabled on port 9000: **F1 → Settings → Connectivity → Client/Server Configuration**.

### Verify your download

This installer is **not yet code-signed**, so Windows will warn about an unrecognised publisher. Until signing is in place the SHA-256 below is the only way to confirm you have the file we built — check it before running:

```powershell
Get-FileHash -Algorithm SHA256 .\{{FILE}}
```

Expected:

```
{{SHA}}
```

If it does not match, do not run the file.

### Verify it was built from this source

Every release carries signed build provenance, so you can confirm the binary was produced by our
release workflow from a specific commit — not just that it matches a hash we published:

```
gh attestation verify .\{{FILE}} -R JINA-CODE-SYSTEMS/tally-mcp-server
```

That is a stronger guarantee than a checksum alone, and it holds even before code signing lands.

### Documentation

[Setup, configuration and the full tool reference](https://github.com/JINA-CODE-SYSTEMS/tally-mcp-server/blob/v{{VERSION}}/docs/README.md).

Where your MCP client runs decides which URL to use — for Claude Desktop on the Tally PC itself, nothing needs to be exposed to the network at all.
